  "body": "As noted by @aethanyc in our [bug 1258657](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1258657#c1), using `display: list-item` for `<summary>` affects other list items.\n\nFor example, the following code:\n\n``` html\n<ol>\n  <li>\n    <details><summary></summary></details>\n  </li>\n  <li></li>\n</ol>\n```\n\nwill produce:\n\n```\n1. ▸\n3.\n```\n\nbecause the [CSS Lists and Counters spec](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-lists-3/#declaring-a-list-item) says: \n\n> list items automatically increment the special list-item counter\n\nBut it should produce:\n\n```\n1. ▸\n2.\n```\n\nThe solution I'd propose is, the spec should say something like:\n\n> details, like ol and ul, resets the list-item counter\n\nand probably add\n\n``` css\ndetails { counter-reset: list-item; }\n```\n\nto the presentational hint as well.\n",
